[font_size=22][b]Welcome to eLogger[/b][/font_size]

eLogger brings [url=https://github.com/Cysharp/ZLogger]ZLogger[/url], the zero-allocation text and structured logger for .NET, to Godot. Enabling the plugin added the [code]ZLogger[/code] and [code]ZString[/code] NuGet packages to your project and made eLogger's runtime code available, so you can start logging right away.

[b]What it does for you[/b]
[ul]
[b]Godot output:[/b] log entries go to the Output panel ([code]GD.Print[/code]), and warnings and errors to the Debugger ([code]GD.PushWarning[/code], [code]GD.PushError[/code]).
[b]Engine messages:[/b] engine, script and shader errors and everything printed through [code]GD.Print[/code] are fed back into ZLogger, under the categories [code]Godot.Engine[/code], [code]Godot.Script[/code], [code]Godot.Shader[/code] and [code]Godot.Output[/code], so they reach every sink you configured.
[b]Readable exceptions:[/b] stack traces are cleaned up and point to [code]res://[/code] paths with line numbers.
[b]ePlugin logging:[/b] in the editor, the messages of ePlugin and the plugins built on it are logged through ZLogger as well.
[/ul]

[b]Where to start[/b]
Add the Godot provider wherever you create your loggers, for example in an autoload:

[code]using Microsoft.Extensions.Logging;
using ZLogger;
using Enaweg.Logger;

using var factory = LoggerFactory.Create(logging =>
{
    logging.SetMinimumLevel(LogLevel.Trace);
    logging.AddZLoggerGodotDebug();
});

var logger = factory.CreateLogger("MyGame");
logger.ZLogInformation($"Player spawned at {position}");[/code]

Formatters, JSON output, filters and other sinks such as [code]AddZLoggerFile[/code] are configured as in plain ZLogger. Use [code]logging.AddFilter("Godot.Output", LogLevel.None)[/code] to stop mirroring [code]GD.Print[/code].

[b]Good to know[/b]
[ul]
Godot 4.5 or newer is required: engine messages are captured through [code]Godot.Logger[/code], which Godot 4.5 introduced.
Disabling eLogger removes the NuGet packages again and hides its runtime code, so game code that uses it no longer compiles.
New eLogger versions are offered in the [b]ePlugin Manager[/b] (ePlugin button on the main toolbar, or [b]Project > Tools > ePlugin Manager...[/b]).
[/ul]

Documentation and source: [url=https://github.com/enaweg/godot-elogger]github.com/enaweg/godot-elogger[/url]
